From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Can Us <me@canus.dev>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Trace skinned and morphed renderables in their current pose

The acceleration structures of 0007 read the vertex buffers, so skinned and
morphed renderables were traced in their bind pose: ray-traced shadows and
ray queries ignored the animation.

A skinned or morphed primitive now gets its own deformable bottom-level
structure, built from a posed copy of its positions. The new driver command
deformAccelerationStructure() records a Vulkan compute pass
(VulkanBlasDeform.comp, precompiled to SPIR-V in VulkanBlasDeformSpirv.h)
that applies the morph target deltas and the four-bone palette exactly as the
vertex shaders do, reading every input by buffer device address (the bone
palette and morph weight uniform buffers get SHADER_DEVICE_ADDRESS usage when
ray queries are on) and the morph target texture through one descriptor; then
it refits the structure (a full build every 32 refits). FScene re-poses a
renderable only in frames its palette or weights changed (a pose version in
FRenderableManager; shared SkinningBuffers every frame) and reports
Scene::getDeformedBlasCount() and the GPU time of the posing passes,
Scene::getLastBlasDeformTimeNanos(). The other backends ignore the command.
---
